---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
---

<BaseLayout
	title="Terms of Use, Financial Disclaimer, and Affiliate Policy | ContractorFX"
	description="Review ContractorFX terms of use, informational fee modeling disclaimers, corridor and KYC rate variance notices, and FTC 16 CFR Part 255 disclosures."
	canonicalPath="/terms/"
>
	<article class="mx-auto max-w-4xl space-y-8">
		<header class="rounded-2xl border border-slate-200 bg-white p-5 sm:p-8 shadow-xs space-y-3">
			<div class="inline-flex flex-wrap items-center gap-2 rounded-full border border-amber-300 bg-amber-50 px-3 py-1 text-xs font-medium text-amber-950">
				<span>Informational Benchmarking Terms</span>
				<span aria-hidden="true">/</span>
				<span>FTC 16 CFR Part 255 Disclosure</span>
			</div>
			<h1 class="text-2xl font-bold tracking-tight text-slate-900 sm:text-4xl">
				Terms of Use and Affiliate Disclosure
			</h1>
			<p class="text-sm leading-relaxed text-slate-600 sm:text-base">
				By accessing or using ContractorFX (<a href="/" class="font-medium text-slate-900 underline hover:text-emerald-800">contractorfx.com</a>), including its interactive FX spread calculators, batch CSV roster auditor, and downloadable routing memos, you agree to the disclaimers and terms set out on this page.
			</p>
		</header>

		<section class="rounded-2xl border border-slate-200 bg-white p-5 sm:p-8 shadow-xs space-y-4">
			<h2 class="text-lg font-bold text-slate-900 sm:text-xl">
				1. Informational Calculator Disclaimer (Not Financial, Tax, or Legal Advice)
			</h2>
			<p class="text-sm leading-relaxed text-slate-700">
				ContractorFX provides mathematical software models and educational payment-routing comparisons strictly for general informational and internal operational planning purposes. Nothing published on ContractorFX or generated by its Markdown (<code>.md</code>) and CSV (<code>.csv</code>) export utilities constitutes financial advice, treasury management advice, foreign exchange brokerage, payment transmission, accounting advice, tax filing guidance, or legal counsel regarding worker classification or Employer of Record compliance.
			</p>
			<p class="text-sm leading-relaxed text-slate-700">
				Cross-border contractor arrangements carry jurisdiction-specific labor, permanent establishment, and tax withholding obligations. Always consult a qualified certified public accountant, treasury specialist, or licensed employment attorney before executing vendor switches or restructuring international contractor contracts.
			</p>
		</section>

		<section class="rounded-2xl border border-slate-200 bg-white p-5 sm:p-8 shadow-xs space-y-4">
			<h2 class="text-lg font-bold text-slate-900 sm:text-xl">
				2. Live Checkout Rate Variance by Corridor and KYC Tier
			</h2>
			<p class="text-sm leading-relaxed text-slate-700">
				All fee estimates, SaaS per-seat rates, funding surcharges, and reference exchange rates shown on ContractorFX reflect point-in-time baseline models documented in our <a href="/about/" class="font-medium text-slate-900 underline hover:text-emerald-800">Editorial and Tariff Modeling Methodology</a>. Actual settlement totals at live provider checkout will differ based on factors including:
			</p>
			<ul class="list-disc space-y-2 pl-5 text-sm leading-relaxed text-slate-700">
				<li>
					<strong class="text-slate-900">Entity jurisdiction and KYC/KYB tier:</strong> Sender incorporation country, recipient tax residency, account verification status, and business account age change eligible local rails and fee caps.
				</li>
				<li>
					<strong class="text-slate-900">Real-time FX liquidity and weekend spreads:</strong> Interbank exchange rates move every second, and providers frequently widen conversion spreads outside core FX market trading hours or on illiquid pairs.
				</li>
				<li>
					<strong class="text-slate-900">Correspondent bank and local rail deductions:</strong> Intermediary SWIFT banks and domestic receiving banks (across SEPA, ACH, Fedwire, PIX, SPEI, IMPS, and InstaPay) may deduct lifting or receiving charges outside the sending platform's stated fee.
				</li>
				<li>
					<strong class="text-slate-900">Negotiated enterprise volume discounts:</strong> Multi-seat annual SaaS contracts or high-volume FX tiers may reduce effective platform fees below public list prices.
				</li>
			</ul>
			<p class="text-sm leading-relaxed text-slate-700">
				You are solely responsible for verifying the binding exchange rate, total fee disclosure, and recipient bank details inside your chosen payment platform immediately prior to authorizing any funds transfer.
			</p>
		</section>

		<section class="rounded-2xl border border-amber-200 bg-amber-50/60 p-5 sm:p-8 shadow-xs space-y-4">
			<h2 class="text-lg font-bold text-slate-900 sm:text-xl">
				3. FTC 16 CFR Part 255 Affiliate and Commercial Disclosure Policy
			</h2>
			<p class="text-sm leading-relaxed text-slate-800">
				In accordance with the United States Federal Trade Commission rules (<code>16 CFR Part 255</code>, Guides Concerning the Use of Endorsements and Testimonials in Advertising), ContractorFX maintains transparent commercial disclosure across all pages:
			</p>
			<ul class="list-disc space-y-2 pl-5 text-sm leading-relaxed text-slate-800">
				<li>
					<strong class="text-slate-950">Partner compensation:</strong> ContractorFX may participate in official B2B affiliate and partner programs operated by cross-border payout and contractor compliance providers, including Wise (via Partnerize), Deel, Remote, and Payoneer. If you follow an outbound link marked <code>rel="sponsored noopener"</code> and complete a qualifying business onboarding or transfer, ContractorFX may receive a referral commission at zero additional cost to you or your recipients.
				</li>
				<li>
					<strong class="text-slate-950">Algorithmic independence:</strong> Affiliate status has zero influence over the mathematical formulas in <code>src/lib/fx-engine.ts</code>. Every calculator route and CSV audit sorts providers strictly by lowest calculated fee drag in USD, regardless of whether ContractorFX holds an active referral agreement with that provider.
				</li>
				<li>
					<strong class="text-slate-950">Explicit link labeling:</strong> Commercial partner links are always accompanied by clear visual disclosure text and HTML <code>rel="sponsored noopener"</code> attributes. No unapproved or disguised redirect parameters are injected.
				</li>
			</ul>
		</section>

		<section class="rounded-2xl border border-slate-200 bg-white p-5 sm:p-8 shadow-xs space-y-4">
			<h2 class="text-lg font-bold text-slate-900 sm:text-xl">
				4. Warranty Disclaimer, Limitation of Liability, and Contact
			</h2>
			<p class="text-sm leading-relaxed text-slate-700">
				ContractorFX and its underlying MIT-licensed open-source calculation models are provided on an "as is" and "as available" basis without warranties of any kind, whether express or implied, including implied warranties of accuracy, merchantability, or fitness for a particular purpose. To the fullest extent permitted by applicable law, ContractorFX and its contributors shall not be liable for any direct, indirect, incidental, consequential, or treasury loss arising from reliance on simulated fee quotes or exported routing memos.
			</p>
			<p class="text-sm leading-relaxed text-slate-700 break-words">
				Review our <a href="/privacy/" class="font-medium text-slate-900 underline hover:text-emerald-800">Privacy Policy</a> for zero-upload data handling details. Direct legal, compliance, or affiliate disclosure inquiries to <a href="mailto:hello@contractorfx.com" class="font-semibold text-slate-900 underline hover:text-emerald-800">hello@contractorfx.com</a>.
			</p>
		</section>
	</article>
</BaseLayout>
